  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:proportional-control",
  "domain": "robotics",
  "definition": "Proportional Control is a feedback control strategy in which the corrective output applied to an actuator is directly proportional to the current error\u2014the difference between the desired setpoint and the measured process variable. It is the foundational component of PID controllers, providing immediate, scaled response to deviations but typically leaving a steady-state offset that requires integral or derivative terms to eliminate.",
